      "writtenOn": "2024-10-23T05:43:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For example, there is a suspend/resume hang case.\nThe call stack is as follows:\n```\n   \u003c0xFFFFFFC0081EF6C8\u003e __switch_to \n   \u003c0xFFFFFFC00923C664\u003e __schedule \n   \u003c0xFFFFFFC00923CA78\u003e schedule \n   \u003c0xFFFFFFC008335CB0\u003e synchronize_irq \n   \u003c0xFFFFFFC008346ED4\u003e suspend_device_irqs \n   \u003c0xFFFFFFC008ACF624\u003e dpm_suspend_noirq \n   \u003c0xFFFFFFC0083210AC\u003e suspend_devices_and_enter \n   \u003c0xFFFFFFC008321958\u003e enter_state \n   ...\n```\n\nThis problem is usually caused by a device driver\u0027s issue. However, we need to find out which device\u0027s IRQ it is waiting for first.\n\nAlthough it is possible to find IRQ information in a Ramdump, it takes a long time. Ramdump may be partially damaged or missing and cannot be analyzed.",
      "parentUuid": "d3957a76_28145d8a",
